<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Ai-Accelerator on Best of AI</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tags/ai-accelerator/</link><description>Recent content in Ai-Accelerator on Best of AI</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-US</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://bestofai.io/tags/ai-accelerator/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Meta MTIA 300</title><link>https://bestofai.io/hardware/meta-mtia-300/</link><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/hardware/meta-mtia-300/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Meta detailed the MTIA 300 on August 24, 2026, its first MTIA chip aimed at large training workloads rather than just inference. It pairs a 12x6 grid of processing elements with 216GB of HBM3E and two network chiplets carrying twelve custom 800 Gbps RDMA NICs, giving each chip 1.2 TB/s of I/O bandwidth so training jobs can scale across racks without relying on separate networking hardware.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Meta MTIA 400</title><link>https://bestofai.io/hardware/meta-mtia-400/</link><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/hardware/meta-mtia-400/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Meta detailed the MTIA 400 at Hot Chips 2026, built on a 3nm process with 288GB of HBM3E and a 1200W TDP. Unlike earlier MTIA chips split into separate training and inference lines, the 400 is built to run both jobs on the same silicon, reaching about 12 petaflops of MXFP4 compute and 6 petaflops at FP8. Meta says it plans to ship a new MTIA generation roughly every six months going forward.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Alibaba Hanguang 800</title><link>https://bestofai.io/hardware/alibaba-hanguang-800/</link><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/hardware/alibaba-hanguang-800/</guid><description/></item><item><title>AWS Inferentia</title><link>https://bestofai.io/hardware/aws-inferentia/</link><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/hardware/aws-inferentia/</guid><description/></item><item><title>AWS Inferentia2</title><link>https://bestofai.io/hardware/aws-inferentia2/</link><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/hardware/aws-inferentia2/</guid><description/></item><item><title>AWS Trainium</title><link>https://bestofai.io/hardware/aws-trainium/</link><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/hardware/aws-trainium/</guid><description/></item><item><title>AWS Trainium2</title><link>https://bestofai.io/hardware/aws-trainium2/</link><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/hardware/aws-trainium2/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Baidu Kunlun II</title><link>https://bestofai.io/hardware/baidu-kunlun-ii/</link><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/hardware/baidu-kunlun-ii/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Cambricon MLU370-X8</title><link>https://bestofai.io/hardware/cambricon-mlu370-x8/</link><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/hardware/cambricon-mlu370-x8/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Cambricon MLU590</title><link>https://bestofai.io/hardware/cambricon-mlu590/</link><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/hardware/cambricon-mlu590/</guid><description/></item><item><title>d-Matrix Corsair</title><link>https://bestofai.io/hardware/d-matrix-corsair/</link><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/hardware/d-matrix-corsair/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Etched Sohu</title><link>https://bestofai.io/hardware/etched-sohu/</link><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/hardware/etched-s